---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
---

<PageLayout
  title="About 50 Five-Star Hotels | Luxury Travel Without Luxury Prices"
  description="About 50 Five-Star Hotels — a luxury editorial travel project built around the idea that five-star comfort can cost far less than most travellers expect."
>
  <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none
    prose-headings:font-serif prose-headings:text-[#1F2428]
    prose-h1:text-4xl prose-h1:mb-8
    prose-h2:text-2xl prose-h2:mt-10 prose-h2:mb-4
    prose-p:text-[#1F2428]/75 prose-p:leading-relaxed
    prose-strong:text-[#1F2428]
    prose-a:text-[#B88A44] prose-a:no-underline hover:prose-a:underline">

    <p class="text-[#B88A44] text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest not-prose mb-4">The project</p>
    <h1>About 50 Five-Star Hotels</h1>

    <p>
      50 Five-Star Hotels is a luxury-value travel project built around a simple idea: in the right cities, five-star comfort can cost far less than most travellers expect.
    </p>
    <p>
      The site looks for hotels where price, place and experience come together — heritage hotels, design hotels, spa hotels, city hotels and resort-style stays that can make a trip feel more special without normal luxury pricing.
    </p>
    <p>
      The goal is not to list the cheapest rooms. The goal is to find hotels that make a traveller think: I did not realise I could have this kind of stay at that price.
    </p>

    <h2>The collection</h2>
    <p>
      The launch collection covers 20 hotels across Southeast Asia, Europe, the Middle East and the Caucasus. All are selected through a structured evaluation process that weights price-to-value, hotel character, review consistency, location quality and nearby destination appeal. Future updates will expand the collection towards 50 hotels.
    </p>

    <h2>What this site is not</h2>
    <p>
      This site is not a hotel booking engine, a comparison tool or an affiliate directory built to maximise link clicks. It is an editorial travel guide. Hotels are included because the editorial case for them is strong, not because they generate commission.
    </p>
    <p>
      It is also not a guarantee of prices. Rates change constantly and every price reference on the site is approximate. Always check current availability for your specific dates before making any travel decision.
    </p>

    <h2>The five-star question</h2>
    <p>
      Not every hotel here is a conventionally luxurious five-star property. Some are heritage hotels rated five-star by local or booking-platform standards, where the value case is interesting even if the polish is not flawless. The site is honest about these distinctions — every profile explains what kind of five-star the hotel is and what that means in practice.
    </p>

    <div class="not-prose mt-12 bg-[#1F2428] rounded-2xl p-8 text-white">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl font-bold mb-3">Start exploring</h2>
      <p class="text-white/60 text-sm mb-6">Browse the collection by destination, budget tier or our top-ranked hotels.</p>
      <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3">
        <a href="/destinations" class="inline-flex items-center bg-[#B88A44] text-white font-semibold py-2.5 px-5 rounded-xl hover:bg-[#A8763A] transition-colors no-underline text-sm">
          Browse by destination
        </a>
        <a href="/under-100" class="inline-flex items-center bg-[#FFFDF8]/10 text-white font-semibold py-2.5 px-5 rounded-xl hover:bg-[#FFFDF8]/20 transition-colors no-underline text-sm">
          Hotels under €100
        </a>
        <a href="/methodology" class="inline-flex items-center bg-[#FFFDF8]/10 text-white font-semibold py-2.5 px-5 rounded-xl hover:bg-[#FFFDF8]/20 transition-colors no-underline text-sm">
          How we choose hotels
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</PageLayout>
